# WFORMTZ.KEY - the form of a key: its memo's load fails as it opens,
# said in a box; ESC leaves it at once, unasked, though NAME holds a
# character the Windows set lacks, and again after blanks typed after
# the key's value, which are not part of it; the memo that failed to
# load stays read-only, typing in it changing nothing; a save refused as
# a duplicate with no field named puts the focus on the key, CODE; a
# save refused for want of a login ends the dialog with WF_LOGIN, which
# the title gives as "KEY 3"; TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WFORMTZ.SNP.
K CTRL-F7
S LOADFAIL
K ENTER
S KEY
K ESC
S KEYESC
K CTRL-F7 ENTER END SPACE SPACE ESC
S BLANKESC
K CTRL-F7 ENTER CTRL-TAB
T x
S MEMORO
K CTRL-TAB TAB
T abc
S NAMED
K ENTER
S DUP
K ENTER
S LOGIN
K ENTER
S KEYEND
